orgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>Last week, John Geddes, a leg=
endary New York Times journalist, died. You may not have heard of John. His=
 byline wasn=E2=80=99t on the front page. He was a managing editor who did =
his magic behind the scenes.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px ge=
orgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>I first met John in 2004. I w=
as a young wire reporter dying to work for The Times. He was my final inter=
view in a lengthy hiring process. Sitting across from me in his office, he =
looked at me over his glasses and asked me the toughest interview question =
I=E2=80=99ve ever gotten: What=E2=80=99s the biggest mistake you=E2=80=99ve=
 made as a journalist=3F</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgi=
a,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>As it happened, I did have a big =
regret.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#33=
3;margin:0 0 15px"><span>The first election I ever covered was the French p=
residential election two years before. The two main candidates, a conservat=
ive and a socialist, were neck and neck heading into the first round, as us=
ual.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;m=
argin:0 0 15px"><span>Like any good wire reporter, I had written stories in=
 advance for what I thought were the two possible outcomes =E2=80=94 the co=
nservative coming first and the socialist coming second, or the socialist c=
oming first and the conservative coming second. After all, that=E2=80=99s w=
hat always happened.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,se=
rif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>That, of course, was the election whe=
n Jean-Marie Le Pen, the father of Marine Le Pen, a far-right nationalist, =
came in second, and made the runoff. No pre-written story for that one.</sp=
an></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 =
0 15px"><span>My mistake had been to expect the expected. (Luckily for me, =
most of my competition did the same thing.)</span></p><p style=3D"font:norm=
al 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>The Times gave=
 me my biggest professional break by hiring me. John=E2=80=99s question als=
o taught me an important lesson: Good journalism requires being radically o=
pen-minded. These days, Marine Le Pen is the front-runner. Does that mean s=
he will win=3F Judging by this week=E2=80=99s election surprises in Brazil =
